title: 'C seam: type the op-complete payload at the ev boundary'
updated: 2026-11-14T18:03:16Z
---

canlin_ev_op_complete(ev, h, status, void *payload, bytes, release) carries an untyped payload. src/module/module.c map_op casts d->payload to const canlin_module_result * with no type tag, so a second producer with a different payload shape would be read wrongly. Latent today: the only producer is src/llm/llm.c:897, which passes the correct type, and include/canlin/module.h:67 documents the contract in prose only. Done when the payload carries a type tag or a typed wrapper exists. Found by the 2026-11-14 review.
